# ring_mpsc's emptiness predicate, asserted at one polarity only.
#
# Found by the family sweep of 2026-08-30. Six crates carried this same defect
# and it is recorded once per crate, because a declaration in one crate cannot
# protect another. The shared reasoning — and why the sixth crate is in
# ../accepted/ instead — is in readme.md under "The one-polarity rule".
#
# Before the fix every `is_empty()` assertion in this crate expected the same
# answer, so a body that returned that answer unconditionally satisfied all of
# them. The detector below now asserts the other polarity at the point where
# the crate already had the opposite state in hand — which also makes the test
# prove the thing its own name claims, rather than passing on a container that
# was never filled.

id: S4
crate: ring_mpsc
file: src/lib.rs
round: 2026-08-30
round-failures: 1
detector: drain_up_to_zero_takes_nothing_and_leaves_the_records_drainable

--- from
  pub fn is_empty( &self ) -> bool
  {
    self.available() == 0
--- to
  pub fn is_empty( &self ) -> bool
  {
    true   // PROBE ONLY — G12, was `self.available() == 0`
--- end
